      "description": "One row per index in index_id order, a heap first as a HEAP row with no name: type, key and included columns, filter, and the user seeks, scans, lookups and updates the server has counted since it started (sys.dm_db_index_usage_stats) with the last time of each. Reading the usage needs VIEW SERVER STATE (VIEW SERVER PERFORMANCE STATE on SQL Server 2022 and later); without it the usage columns are NULL with a warning. --fragmentation adds each index's fragmentation, page and fragment counts from sys.dm_db_index_physical_stats in that mode — it reads the index, so it is off by default: limited reads the pages above the leaf and has no page fullness; sampled and detailed read the leaf.",
